{"name":"Dark Ebony","hex":"#3d2004","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"ebony","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard, dense, deep black wood from various subtropical and tropical trees, especially of the genus Diospyros.","A tree that yields such wood."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of ebony wood.","A deep, dark black colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ebony"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ebony","blocks":[{"text":"Ebony is a dense black–brown hardwood, coming from several species in the genus Diospyros, which also includes the persimmon. A few Diospyros species, such as macassar and mun ebony, are dense enough to sink in water. Ebony is finely textured and has a mirror finish when polished, making it valuable as an ornamental wood. It is often cited as one of the most expensive woods in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/%C3%89bano.jpg/330px-%C3%89bano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ebony","wikidata":"Q156005"},{"title":"Shades of black","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of black, or off-black colors, are colors that differ only slightly from pure black. These colors have a low lightness. From a photometric point of view, a color which differs slightly from black always has low relative luminance. Colors often considered \"shades of black\" include onyx, black olive, charcoal, and jet."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cc/Color_icon_black_new2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_black","wikidata":"Q7460340"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/%C3%89bano.jpg/330px-%C3%89bano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/%C3%89bano.jpg/330px-%C3%89bano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cross-section of an unprocessed piece of ebony wood","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%C3%89bano.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/EbonyLabelOfDen-BritishMuseum-August19-08.jpg/500px-EbonyLabelOfDen-BritishMuseum-August19-08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/EbonyLabelOfDen-BritishMuseum-August19-08.jpg/1280px-EbonyLabelOfDen-BritishMuseum-August19-08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/EbonyLabelOfDen-BritishMuseum-August19-08.jpg/500px-EbonyLabelOfDen-BritishMuseum-August19-08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ebony label depicting the pharaoh Den, found in his tomb in Abydos, circa 3000 BC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEbonyLabelOfDen-BritishMuseum-August19-08.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Ebony_elefant.JPG/500px-Ebony_elefant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Ebony_elefant.JPG/500px-Ebony_elefant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Elephant carvings from Sri Lanka, probably Gabon ebony (D. crassiflora)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEbony_elefant.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Bellpianokeyboarddetail%